      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this needs to be an opt-in feature, because it could break existing logs authentication in certain configuration. For example, if the logs are protected with mod_auth_openidc in Apache reverse proxy with \u0027AuthType auth-openidc\u0027, that configured to be authorized if either an oidc session exists or a valid \"Authorization: Bear\" token that can be only verified by configured `OIDCOAuthVerifySharedKeys`.\nIn this case, the added Authorization header could not be verified and would cause `Unauthorized\u0027 error.",
